<description>
Paint the longest black diagonal segment teal, choosing the middle segment when the longest run is an odd-width parallel band.

Input structure
A 10x10 grid containing black pixels embedded in a grey field/frame.

Rule
Find every maximal contiguous black segment along both diagonal directions. Select the maximum-length segment; if the maximum-length candidates form adjacent parallel diagonals, select the central diagonal of that band. Recolor the selected black pixels to teal.

Key insight
The output marks the hidden straight diagonal stroke inside the black mask; the only ambiguous training case is a three-diagonal band, where the centered parallel run is the marked stroke.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "maximal contiguous black runs in either 45-degree diagonal orientation inside the grey frame",
  "transform": "recolor the longest run teal and preserve all other pixels",
  "multi_step": "if multiple longest runs are adjacent parallel diagonals, choose the central run of the band"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10x10, border always grey(5), interior cells rows 1-8, cols 1-8
  colors: input has only black(0) and grey(5); output adds teal(8)
  black_blob:
    single 4-connected component, entirely within rows 1-8 / cols 1-8
    cell_count: 39-48 (fraction of 64 interior cells ~61-75%)
    no black on the grid border (row 0/9, col 0/9)
  diagonal_runs: maximal contiguous black segments along NE or SE diagonals
    winning_orientation: one of (1,1) or (1,-1), strictly longer max than the other
    cross_orientation_gap: >=1 [observed >=1, typically 1-2]
    max_run_length: 6-8
    candidates: odd count (1 or 3) of same-max-length parallel runs on consecutive diagonals
    second_longest_run: max_run_length minus 1-2
  transform: recolor the central candidate diagonal's cells from black to teal(8)
    if 1 candidate, that is the answer; if 3, pick the middle diagonal
    teal_count equals max_run_length

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first then invert
  steps:
    1. Pick orientation (1,1) or (1,-1) and band_width in {1, 3}
    2. Pick max_run_length L in 6-8; place L-cell answer diagonal fully inside rows 1-8 / cols 1-8
    3. If band_width=3, place two flanking parallel diagonals of length L on adjacent diag-ids
    4. Build a connected black blob around the answer diagonal by flood-growing black cells
       in the interior, reaching 39-48 total black cells, keeping 4-connectivity
    5. Ensure no other diagonal run (either orientation) reaches length L;
       trim any that do by flipping one cell to grey
    6. Replace teal cells with black to produce the input grid
```
